{"authored" [{"question" "q-73659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{x{log}_{7}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{7}⁡(4x).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x{log}_{7}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{log}_{7}⁡(4x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{7}⁡(4x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "88b04a28acd4d8c79e101e9c9e9690d5266f0dc014b1b37dc30f9e50b76e5a87" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73659" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{3{log}_{6}^{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{6}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{log}_{6}^{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int ({log}_{6}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "88b04a28acd4d8c79e101e9c9e9690d5266f0dc014b1b37dc30f9e50b76e5a87" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{3}\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "0954e2dcc1963f75a4f6bfee5962ea7b629c861f87b01fccab2ecd7cac532731" "basis" 1351 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-13841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e/2}^{{e}^{2}/2}\\frac{2}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-13841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2x}\\cdot 2=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e/2$ | ${e}^{2}/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e/2}^{{e}^{2}/2}\\frac{2}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{e/2}^{{e}^{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-13841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6b9dd97b5feca6bb8daa5aa762c6e122276f1a8b769932d775323ba90d448fa"} {"question" "q-13841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-13841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-13841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-49605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-49605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then  we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$  gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | ${e}^{2}$ | ${e}^{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{2}^{4}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {u}^{2}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (16-4) \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-49605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6b9dd97b5feca6bb8daa5aa762c6e122276f1a8b769932d775323ba90d448fa"} {"question" "q-49605" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-49605" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4"] ["math" "48"] ["math" "68"] ["math" "{ln}^{2}⁡2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-49605" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "48"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-73653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{4{log}_{4}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-73653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{4}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{4{log}_{4}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{1}^{4}{log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡4{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040971/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bdcec04c9c97a12a16c1e9aa17483de614629a792cd2617e70904dfe1d450ab"} {"question" "q-73653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1